WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.950
Two stone tablets.

2
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:05.660
A handful of short commands:
you shall not murder,

3
00:00:05.710 --> 00:00:07.300
you shall not steal.

4
00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:13.290
For many Christians, these words from Exodus
20 are still the basis of moral teaching.

5
00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:17.560
In Matthew 5 to 7, Jesus
teaches: love your enemies,

6
00:00:17.610 --> 00:00:20.170
and pray for those who persecute you.

7
00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:24.650
But the Bible is silent on
genetic engineering and on AI.

8
00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:28.980
Can a book written thousands of
years ago still tell us how to live?

9
00:00:29.030 --> 00:00:33.170
In this mission, you'll read the commands
and see how Christians read the Sermon

10
00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:34.420
differently.

11
00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:39.200
Then you'll ask whether stories can
teach right and wrong better than rules.

12
00:00:39.250 --> 00:00:44.120
Your mission: weigh up whether an ancient
book can still tell us how to live.
